2026-08-16T02:29:12.3630869Z [36;1m# Infer each compiler default for the active R version from R CMD config,[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3631394Z [36;1m# then route it through ccache. Reading the resolved defaults preserves the[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3631947Z [36;1m# standard flags R selects per version (e.g. -std=gnu2x for C, -std=gnu++17[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3632458Z [36;1m# / -std=gnu++20 for C++); a plain "CC = ccache gcc" override would drop[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3632947Z [36;1m# them and silently downgrade the standard across the version matrix.[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3633454Z [36;1m# Inference uses an empty user Makevars so we always read the pristine[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3633896Z [36;1m# Makeconf defaults, never a value we just wrote.[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3634336Z [36;1m# Note: the versioned switches (CXX11..CXX23) intentionally come out as[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3634802Z [36;1m# bare "g++" with no -std flag. R keeps the standard in a separate[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3635267Z [36;1m# CXXnnSTD variable (CXX17STD = -std=gnu++17, ...) and applies it on top[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3635755Z [36;1m# at compile time, so wrapping only CXXnn with ccache is correct and we[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3636146Z [36;1m# must NOT pin -std here ourselves.[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3636403Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3636682Z [36;1m# On Unix, ccache is attached through a generated one-word wrapper[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3637141Z [36;1m# command (ccache-gcc, ccache-g++, ...) rather than the more obvious[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3637596Z [36;1m# "CC = ccache gcc" prefix. R-devel briefly could not cope with a[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3638258Z [36;1m# compiler command of more than one word: tools:::ccE(), which backs the[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3638761Z [36;1m# "checking use of non-API entry points" check and therefore runs for[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3639675Z [36;1m# every package with compiled code, read R CMD config CC, kept only the[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3640157Z [36;1m# first word, and ran that. With "CC = ccache gcc" that left a bare[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3640611Z [36;1m# "ccache", and the check died with "ccache: invalid option -- 'E'".[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3641145Z [36;1m# https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/commit/ca19f35240517186ed447e773ee67b55e207cf27[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3641642Z [36;1m# https://bugs.r-project.org/show_bug.cgi?id=19130[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3642087Z [36;1m# Upstream has since dropped the truncation again, so the prefix works[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3642584Z [36;1m# once more -- but it takes a while for that to reach the R-devel builds[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3643056Z [36;1m# CI installs, so the wrapper is still doing real work here. It stays[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3643493Z [36;1m# after that too: it costs nothing and is correct either way.[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3643994Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3644298Z [36;1m# Windows deliberately keeps the plain prefix, as a control group: it is[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3644789Z [36;1m# where a repeat of that upstream change would show up, while the Unix[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3645161Z [36;1m# jobs carry on regardless.[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3645442Z [36;1mccache_bin="$(command -v ccache || true)"[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3645728Z [36;1mif [ -z "$ccache_bin" ]; then[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3646088Z [36;1m  echo "::warning::ccache is not on the PATH, compiling without it."[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3646440Z [36;1melse[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3646649Z [36;1m  wrapper_dir="$HOME/.R/ccache-wrappers"[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3646951Z [36;1m  if [ "$RUNNER_OS" != "Windows" ]; then[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3647229Z [36;1m    mkdir -p "$wrapper_dir"[0m
