2026-08-16T02:29:12.3661740Z [36;1m# Compile on every core the runner has, not the two this used to pin.[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3662229Z [36;1m# Standard GitHub-hosted Linux runners have been 4-vCPU since 2024, so[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3662708Z [36;1m# -j2 left half the box idle through the phase that dominates a build:[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3663168Z [36;1m# measured on a 4-core box, 8 vendored unity objects with ccache[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3663606Z [36;1m# disabled take 70.8 s at -j2 and 43.1 s at -j4 -- 1.64x, at identical[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3664068Z [36;1m# user time. Peak RSS per unity object is ~834 MB, so four in flight is[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3664433Z [36;1m# ~3.3 GB of the runner's 16 GB.[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3664792Z [36;1m# detectCores() can return NA on exotic platforms; fall back to the old[0m
2026-08-16T02:29:12.3665265Z [36;1m# value there. `--as-cran` sets _R_CHECK_LIMIT_CORES_, but that polices[0m
